libmpeg2 0.5.1 -- vendored decoder core
=======================================

Source:  https://deb.debian.org/debian/pool/main/m/mpeg2dec/mpeg2dec_0.5.1.orig.tar.gz
         (the upstream release tarball, libmpeg2-0.5.1/, as Debian ships it)
SHA-256: dee22e893cb5fc2b2b6ebd60b88478ab8556cb3b93f9a0d7ce8f3b61851871d4
Licence: GPL-2.0-or-later (COPYING), compatible with this repository's GPL-3.

Used by tools/fmvbench (phase 1 of docs/fmv-plan.md) to measure MPEG-1
decoding on the MiSTer's ARM, and since phase 3 by Main itself, as the CD32
FMV module's video decoder (support/minimig/fmv_decoder.cpp). The top-level
Makefile builds the portable C files only, not motion_comp_arm*: phase 1
measured the ARM assembler at no gain. tests/Makefile builds the same files
for test_fmv_decoder, without sanitizers (slice.c left-shifts negative
values, which UBSan reports and GCC defines).

Taken, unchanged:
  COPYING AUTHORS README
  include/mpeg2.h include/attributes.h
  libmpeg2/{alloc,cpu_accel,cpu_state,decode,header,idct,motion_comp,slice}.c
  libmpeg2/motion_comp_arm.c libmpeg2/motion_comp_arm_s.S
  libmpeg2/mpeg2_internal.h libmpeg2/vlc.h

Left out: the autoconf build, libvo, the convert/ library (fmvbench does its
own YUV -> RGB565, since that is the format the core will scan out), the
mpeg2dec/extract programs, and the x86/PPC/Alpha/SPARC acceleration files.

Added: config.h, written by hand in place of the autoconf one (see the file).

To check the copy against the tarball:
  tar xzf mpeg2dec_0.5.1.orig.tar.gz
  for f in $(cd lib/libmpeg2 && find include libmpeg2 -type f); do
    cmp libmpeg2-0.5.1/$f lib/libmpeg2/$f; done
